Mixed DML — setup + non-setup

The scenario: creating a Contact (non-setup) and assigning a permission set to a User (setup) in one flow.

public with sharing class PortalOnboardingService {

    // Entry point — synchronous, non-setup DML only.
    public static void onboard(Contact c, Id userId, String permSetName) {

        insert c;                                    // non-setup DML

        // Deferred to its own transaction. Attempting the PermissionSetAssignment
        // inline here throws MIXED_DML_OPERATION.
        assignPermissionSet(userId, permSetName, c.Id);
    }

    @future
    private static void assignPermissionSet(Id userId, String permSetName, Id contactId) {

        List<PermissionSet> psList = [
            SELECT Id FROM PermissionSet WHERE Name = :permSetName LIMIT 1
        ];

        if (psList.isEmpty()) {
            logFailure(contactId, 'Permission set not found: ' + permSetName);
            return;
        }

        // Idempotency — the future may be retried, and a duplicate
        // assignment throws DUPLICATE_VALUE.
        Integer existing = [
            SELECT COUNT()
            FROM PermissionSetAssignment
            WHERE AssigneeId = :userId AND PermissionSetId = :psList[0].Id
        ];

        if (existing > 0) {
            return;
        }

        Database.SaveResult sr = Database.insert(
            new PermissionSetAssignment(
                AssigneeId = userId,
                PermissionSetId = psList[0].Id
            ),
            false
        );

        if (!sr.isSuccess()) {
            logFailure(contactId, sr.getErrors()[0].getMessage());
        }
    }

    private static void logFailure(Id contactId, String msg) {
        Database.insert(new Integration_Log__c(
            Record_Id__c  = contactId,
            Error_Type__c = 'PermSetAssignment',
            Detail__c     = msg
        ), false);
    }
}

The direction of the split is a real choice. Here the non-setup DML stays synchronous and the setup DML goes async — right when the Contact is what the user is waiting on. If the setup work is the thing that must succeed for the user to log in, invert it: do the setup DML synchronously and defer the Contact insert.

